{%- comment -%}
  DEPRECATED — intentionally a no-op.

  This snippet used to intercept form[action="/search"] submits, call the
  worker /search-nl endpoint to translate the query into Shopify literal-search
  keywords, show a blocking overlay, then redirect. That whole path is obsolete:

  Search is now SEMANTIC. The search form submits the RAW user query to
  /search?q=<query>; the search results section (lm-search-chat.liquid) reads
  ?q= and POSTs it to the worker /api/search, which embeds the raw query with
  multilingual BGE-M3 (Chinese works directly — no keyword translation needed)
  and ranks against the Vectorize index.

  Keeping the old interceptor caused a double round-trip (translate+redirect,
  then embed) and rewrote the query before semantic search saw it. Removed.

  Left as an empty render target so existing {% render 'wp-search-nl' %} calls
  across the theme stay valid without re-pushing every section.
{%- endcomment -%}
